    "explanation": "# Release build: @appport/resolver 0.4.2, @appport/resolver-client 0.3.1, @appport/resolver-core 0.2.1\n\nBuild, test and package release commit df70ca12d7baf95dbf157b8352c589af702683b7 for Boundry Maintenance release appport-resolver@0.4.2.\n\nRecipe `.boundry/recipes/boundry-release.md` · sha256:683adf3b3a33 · compiled by boundry-recipes/1.0.0 with boundry-capabilities/1.0.1 · definition bd87b71702d9\n\n## Runs when\n- an authorized person starts it\n\n## Project\n- Node.js project using npm (`package-lock.json`) in the repository root (evidence: `package-lock.json`, `package.json`)\n\n## Checks (one job)\n1. **The tests pass** — runs `npm test`\n   Node.js 22 · installs dependencies first · internet: yes · keeps `test-results.txt` · capability `check.tests@1.0.0`\n\n## Steps (in order, after every check passes)\n1. **Package the result** — runs `npm run build`, then `npm pack --workspaces`\n   Node.js 22 · installs dependencies first · internet: yes · keeps `package.tar` · capability `step.package@1.0.0`\n\n## Authority\n- Permissions: none\n- Secrets: none\n- Approvals: none\n- Publishes or deploys: nothing\n- Proposed changes from forks never receive secrets, release/deploy access or trusted caches.\n\n## Kept\n- `package.tar` from “Package the result” for 3650 days\n- `test-results.txt` from “The tests pass” for 30 days (also when tests fail)\n- The record: this recipe, its compiled plan, project facts, every attempt's log, inputs and outputs (always)\n\n## Afterward\n- Nothing is reported to GitHub (add “Report the result on the change” to do so)\n",
